  <h2>How To Run</h2>
  <p>Install dependencies if needed:</p>
  <pre>npm install</pre>

  <p>Start the development server:</p>
  <pre>npm run dev -- --host 127.0.0.1</pre>

  <p>Open this URL in a browser:</p>
  <pre>http://127.0.0.1:5173/</pre>

  <p>Build for production:</p>
  <pre>npm run build</pre>

  <p>PowerShell note: if npm.ps1 is blocked by execution policy, use npm.cmd:</p>
  <pre>npm.cmd run build</pre>

  <p>Preview the production build:</p>
  <pre>npm run preview</pre>

  <h2>Deployment Workflow</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Development work should be committed and pushed to develop unless the user explicitly asks for main.</li>
    <li>AWS Amplify pipeline exists for the main branch.</li>
    <li>The user prefers to merge or pull code into main manually.</li>
    <li>Do not push main automatically unless the user explicitly asks.</li>
    <li>Amplify build settings are stored in amplify.yml.</li>
    <li>Amplify runs npm ci and npm run build, then deploys the dist directory.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Current App Content</h2>
  <p>
    The app presents orilto.ai as an AI-first product studio that helps businesses
    with AI websites, AI systems, automation, technical support, social operations,
    and new innovation builds.
  </p>

  <h3>Main Landing Page Sections</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>Header navigation: Services, Systems, Studio, Contact.</li>
    <li>Hero section: "The technical layer modern businesses need to grow."</li>
    <li>Operating layer visual: connected business nodes for website, leads, automation, support, and content.</li>
    <li>Proof strip: business-first technical thinking, design/build/automate/support, practical outcomes.</li>
    <li>Problem section: before/after comparison between scattered technical work and a connected operating layer.</li>
    <li>Services section: AI Websites, AI Systems, Workflow Automation, Technical Support, Social Media Support, Innovation Builds.</li>
    <li>Use cases section: website launch, automation, AI assistant/internal tool, technical operations support.</li>
    <li>Studio model section: diagnose, map, prototype, build/connect, launch/support/improve.</li>
    <li>CTA section: "Bring the business problem. We will shape the technical system."</li>
    <li>Footer: brand summary, studio links, contact links.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Contact Page Details</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>Route: /contact</li>
    <li>Main goal: Encourage users to describe a business problem that orilto.ai can turn into a technical system.</li>
    <li>Form fields: name, email, need, and brief.</li>
    <li>Direct email: hello@orilto.ai</li>
    <li>Contact reasons: better website or product surface, automation, AI support/content/operations tooling, technical help with a product-studio brain.</li>
    <li>Form behavior: opens the user's email app using mailto because no backend is currently connected.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Design Direction</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Current direction name: orilto.ai Operating Layer.</li>
    <li>Visual personality: AI-first product studio, technical, sharp, business-oriented, and practical.</li>
    <li>Palette: deep graphite/near-black base, soft white text, electric cyan, green system status, and limited supporting accent colors.</li>
    <li>Typography: modern sans-serif using Manrope.</li>
    <li>Layout principle: fewer generic cards, stronger system visual, more operational storytelling.</li>
    <li>Hero visual: custom CSS interface mockup showing business nodes connected around an AI studio core.</li>
    <li>Motion: lightweight CSS floating motion on system nodes with reduced motion support.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>File Map</h2>
  <table>
    <tr>
      <th>Path</th>
      <th>Description</th>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>package.json</td>
      <td>Defines scripts and dependencies for the React/Vite app.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>amplify.yml</td>
      <td>AWS Amplify build workflow. Runs npm ci and npm run build, deploys dist.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>vite.config.js</td>
      <td>Configures Vite with the React plugin.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>index.html</td>
      <td>HTML shell used by Vite.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>src/main.jsx</td>
      <td>React entry point. Mounts the App component into the root element.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>src/App.jsx</td>
      <td>Main React component. Contains homepage, contact page, data arrays, and content structure.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>src/App.css</td>
      <td>Main page styling and responsive visual system for the orilto.ai website.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>src/index.css</td>
      <td>Global CSS imported by the React entry point, including font import and global defaults.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>public/</td>
      <td>Static public assets.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>dist/</td>
      <td>Production build output generated by Vite. Ignored by git.</td>
    </tr>
  </table>

  <h2>Dependencies</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>react</li>
    <li>react-dom</li>
    <li>vite</li>
    <li>@vitejs/plugin-react</li>
    <li>eslint and React ESLint plugins</li>
  </ul>

